	128-255	ID number of a specific dude class\
\
ShipGoal	The mission goal associated with the special ships\
\cf2 	-1	Ignored (no specific goal for the special ships)\cf0 \
	0	Destroy all the ships\
	\cf2 1	Disable but don't destroy them\cf0 \
	2	Board them\
	\cf2 3	Escort them (keep them from getting killed)\cf0 \
	4	Observe them (you just have to be in the same system with them)\
	\cf2 5	Rescue them (they start out disabled, and you must board them)\cf0 \
	6	Chase them off (either kill them or scare the into jumping out of the system)\
\
ShipBehav	Defines any special actions you want the ships to take\
\cf2 	-1	Ignored (they use their standard AI routines)\
\cf0 	0	Special ships will always attack the player\
	\cf2 1	Special ships will protect the player\cf0 \
	9	Special ships will hyper in all together after a short delay\
	\cf2 10	Special ships will hyper in and attack the player\cf0 \
	11	Special ships will hyper in and protect the player\
\
ShipNameID	Tells Override how to name the special ships\
	-1		Ignored (special ships have normal names)\
	128 and up	Pick a name from this STR# resource\
\
\
The next three fields determine what will happen when you successfully complete the mission:\
\
CompBitSet		Which mission bit will be set on completion\
\cf2 	-1		Ignored\cf0 \
	0-511		Set this mission bit\
\cf2 	1000-1511	Clear this mission bit\cf0 \
